Xeen: show direction and position when it is too dark to see

Without light in a dark maze the 3D view is filled black, so a step or a
turn changes nothing on the screen; on e-ink there is no feedback at all.
Write "Too dark to see" with the facing and the map position into the
view (window 3, like door and sign text) while the scene is black and no
monsters are being fought.

--- a/engines/mm/xeen/interface.cpp
+++ b/engines/mm/xeen/interface.cpp
@@ -1373,6 +1373,15 @@
 		_ttsPreviousScreenText = _screenText;
 	} else {
 		_ttsPreviousScreenText.clear();
+
+		// mmIV: without light the view is all black, so a step or turn
+		// changes nothing on screen. Show where the party stands instead.
+		if (_obscurity == OBSCURITY_BLACK && combat._attackMonsters[0] == -1) {
+			windows[3].writeString(Common::String::format(
+				"\f15\x03""c\t116\v056Too dark to see\n%s  %d, %d\x03""l\fd",
+				Res.DIRECTION_TEXT[party._mazeDirection],
+				party._mazePosition.x, party._mazePosition.y), false);
+		}
 	}
 
 	if (updateFlag) {
